      "writtenOn": "2017-06-15T05:32:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "per this logic, to me it looks like for non-prefer_idle tasks, we will always select a best_idle_cpu if atleast one of the CPUs were in a idle state. Shouldn\u0027t the approach be the other way around, for non-prefer_idle tasks - we should try to pack the task on an available CPU before looking into idle ones?",
